The LCG has full period, so each random section is a repeating cycle that I build once and then output in precomputed blocks.

- **Full period:** the modulus is 139968 = 2⁶·3⁷, the multiplier satisfies a−1 = 3876 = 2²·3·17·19, and the increment 29573 is coprime to the modulus. By the Hull–Dobell conditions the period is exactly 139968.
- **Symbol lookup:** for each possible seed value v I pick the first symbol whose cumulative probability exceeds v/139968. That gives a lookup table indexed by seed, so no per-draw search is needed.
- **Cycle strings:** I generate the 139968 seeds once, starting from 42. Section 2's cycle maps each seed in order through table 2. Section 3 continues from the seed state after 3N draws, so its cycle starts at index 3N mod 139968 and maps through table 3.
- **Wrapped blocks:** for any cycle of length `len`, I repeat it `lcm(len, 60)/len` times and wrap at 60 columns. This gives a block that tiles exactly. The ALU block is 17220 characters and the random-section blocks are 699840 characters.
- **Output:** I echo the full blocks, then a prefix of the block for the remainder, adding a final newline if the last line is short.

```php
<?php
$N = (int)$argv[1];
$P = 139968;

function gcd($a, $b) { while ($b) { $t = $a % $b; $a = $b; $b = $t; } return $a; }

function emit($C, $L) {
    $len = strlen($C);
    $g = gcd($len, 60);
    $lcm = intdiv($len, $g) * 60;
    $block = chunk_split(str_repeat($C, intdiv($lcm, $len)), 60, "\n");
    $blen = strlen($block);
    $full = intdiv($L, $lcm);
    for ($i = 0; $i < $full; $i++) {
        echo $block;
    }
    $r = $L - $full * $lcm;
    if ($r > 0) {
        $s = substr($block, 0, $r + intdiv($r, 60));
        if ($r % 60 != 0) $s .= "\n";
        echo $s;
    }
}

function buildLookup($syms, $probs, $P) {
    $n = count($syms);
    $cum = [];
    $p = 0.0;
    for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) { $p += $probs[$i]; $cum[$i] = $p; }
    $lk = [];
    for ($v = 0; $v < $P; $v++) {
        $r = $v / $P;
        $c = $syms[$n - 1];
        for ($i = 0; $i < $n; $i++) {
            if ($cum[$i] > $r) { $c = $syms[$i]; break; }
        }
        $lk[$v] = $c;
    }
    return $lk;
}

$alu = "GGCCGGGCGCGGTGGCTCACGCCTGTAATCCCAGCACTTTGGGAGGCCGAGGCGGGCGGA"
     . "TCACCTGAGGTCAGGAGTTCGAGACCAGCCTGGCCAACATGGTGAAACCCCGTCTCTACT"
     . "AAAAATACAAAAATTAGCCGGGCGTGGTGGCGCGCGCCTGTAATCCCAGCTACTCGGGAG"
     . "GCTGAGGCAGGAGAATCGCTTGAACCCGGGAGGCGGAGGTTGCAGTGAGCCGAGATCGCG"
     . "CCACTGCACTCCAGCCTGGGCGACAGAGCGAGACTCCGTCTCAAAAA";

$lk2 = buildLookup(
    ['a','c','g','t','B','D','H','K','M','N','R','S','V','W','Y'],
    [0.27,0.12,0.12,0.27,0.02,0.02,0.02,0.02,0.02,0.02,0.02,0.02,0.02,0.02,0.02],
    $P);
$lk3 = buildLookup(['a','c','g','t'],
    [0.3029549426680,0.1979883004921,0.1975473066391,0.3015094502008], $P);

$seeds = [];
$s = 42;
for ($i = 0; $i < $P; $i++) {
    $s = ($s * 3877 + 29573) % $P;
    $seeds[$i] = $s;
}

$c2 = '';
$parts = [];
for ($i = 0; $i < $P; $i++) $parts[] = $lk2[$seeds[$i]];
$c2 = implode('', $parts);

$off = (3 * $N) % $P;
$parts = [];
for ($i = 0; $i < $P; $i++) {
    $j = $off + $i;
    if ($j >= $P) $j -= $P;
    $parts[] = $lk3[$seeds[$j]];
}
$c3 = implode('', $parts);

echo ">ONE Homo sapiens alu\n";
emit($alu, 2 * $N);
echo ">TWO IUB ambiguity codes\n";
emit($c2, 3 * $N);
echo ">THREE Homo sapiens frequency\n";
emit($c3, 5 * $N);
```

