- The IUPAC table is applied with `strtr` over a 256-entry translation, and lowercase letters map to the same complements.
- The original line width is 60 in the benchmark. To honor "preserving line-wrapping" more generally, I detect the width as the length of the first sequence line in each record and use 60 as the default.
- Each record is parsed by finding the header line and removing the newlines from the rest of the record.
- The complement table is: A→T, C→G, G→C, T→A, U→A, R→Y, Y→R, K→M, M→K, B→V, V→B, D→H, H→D, and S, W, N map to themselves. Lowercase letters map to the same complement as their uppercase forms (the benchmark's usual behavior).
- `strrev` plus `strtr` is fast for large input. The output is built with `chunk_split` or `substr` loops, then written once per record.
- N is ignored, but `$argv[1]` is accepted without being used.

```php
<?php
$data = stream_get_contents(STDIN);
$from = "ACGTUacgtuRYKMBVDHryk mbvdh";
$from = "ACGTURYKMBVDHSWNacgturykmbvdhswn";
$to   = "TGCAAYRMKVBHDSWNTGCAAYRMKVBHDSWN";
$len = strlen($data);
$pos = 0;
$out = '';
while ($pos < $len) {
    if ($data[$pos] === '>') {
        $nl = strpos($data, "\n", $pos);
        if ($nl === false) {
            $out .= substr($data, $pos) . "\n";
            break;
        }
        $out .= substr($data, $pos, $nl - $pos + 1);
        $pos = $nl + 1;
    }
    $next = strpos($data, "\n>", $pos);
    if ($next === false) {
        $seg = substr($data, $pos);
        $pos = $len;
    } else {
        $seg = substr($data, $pos, $next - $pos + 1);
        $pos = $next + 1;
    }
    // determine width
    $fl = strpos($seg, "\n");
    $width = ($fl === false || $fl == 0) ? 60 : $fl;
    $seq = str_replace(["\n", "\r"], '', $seg);
    if ($seq === '') continue;
    $seq = strtr(strrev($seq), $from, $to);
    $out .= chunk_split($seq, $width, "\n");
    if (strlen($out) > 1 << 22) {
        fwrite(STDOUT, $out);
        $out = '';
    }
}
fwrite(STDOUT, $out);
```

